---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Nakvali"
  description="How Nakvali handles recordings, account information and optional ride sharing."
>
  <article class="document">
    <p class="eyebrow">YOUR DATA</p>
    <h1>Privacy, on the trail.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Your original ride recordings stay on your phone. You choose when to
      export or share them.
    </p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {site.updated}</p>
    <h2>Who runs Nakvali</h2>
    <p>
      Nakvali is an independent cycling recorder developed by Stas, known as{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/whekin">whekin</a>. This notice covers the
      Android app and this website.
    </p>
    {site.contactEmail ? (
      <p>
        For privacy questions or account-data requests, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. Do not
        send GPS recordings or credentials unless needed for a support request
        you choose to make.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="notice">
        Preview: a private contact address must be configured before this page
        is published.
      </p>
    )}
    <h2>Recordings on your phone</h2>
    <p>
      When you start a recording, Nakvali uses location, timestamps and
      available motion and pressure sensors to record and process your ride.
      Recording can continue in the background until you stop it. Tracks, ride
      statistics, sensor recordings and diagnostic files are stored locally.
      Recording and local review do not require an account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Raw GPS, motion and pressure recordings are not automatically uploaded to
      the Nakvali server. They remain on your device until you delete them or
      remove the app. Exports and backups you create may remain in the folders
      or services you choose. Android backup behavior also depends on your
      device settings.
    </p>
    <h2>Optional account and maps</h2>
    <p>
      If you sign in with Google, Firebase Authentication processes the sign-in.
      The Nakvali backend receives your verified account ID, email address,
      display name, avatar URL and email-verification status to maintain your
      profile. Signing out ends the app session; it does not itself delete the
      server-side account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Online map requests go to OpenFreeMap and the resources referenced by its
      map style. Those services receive normal network information, including
      your IP address and the map tiles requested. Previously downloaded map
      data may be cached on your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      See{' '}
      <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy">
        Firebase privacy information
      </a>{' '}
      and{' '}
      <a href="https://openfreemap.org/privacy/">
        OpenFreeMap’s privacy policy
      </a>{' '}
      for how those providers handle their services.
    </p>
    <h2>Exports and connected services</h2>
    <p>
      A GPX or TCX export can contain precise locations, timestamps and
      altitude. Android’s save or share flow sends the file to the destination
      you select. Local diagnostic and backup exports may include raw sensor
      data; share them only with a recipient you intend.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some development builds include an optional Strava connection. If you use
      it, the Nakvali backend stores the connection credentials and export
      status, and sends the processed ride you request to Strava.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>
        BIKEYARD uploads are planned, not available in the current build.
      </strong>{' '}
      The intended flow asks you to connect BIKEYARD and choose uploads or opt
      into automatic uploads of new saved rides. It will send processed tracks
      and selected ride metadata with your chosen visibility. Original sensor
      files will stay on the phone. This notice will be updated when that
      integration is available.
    </p>
    <h2>This website and operational data</h2>
    <p>
      This website contains no analytics scripts, advertising trackers or
      tracking cookies. Its fonts and artwork are served from the same site.
      Hosting and proxy services process connection information such as IP
      addresses, requested paths, response status and timestamps to deliver and
      protect the service. The Nakvali API may retain operational logs for
      troubleshooting.
    </p>
    <p>
      GitHub hosts the source and release downloads. Following a GitHub link or
      downloading a release is subject to{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
        GitHub’s privacy statement
      </a>
      . Nakvali does not sell personal data.
    </p>
    <h2>Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You control local recordings through the app’s delete, export and backup
      actions. Server account information is retained while your account is in
      use or until you request deletion. Operational records are retained only
      as needed for service operation, troubleshooting and security; backup
      copies may take longer to expire. Data you publish to another service is
      managed separately by that service.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can request access, correction or deletion of the account information
      held by Nakvali using the private contact above. You can also ask about
      retention and processing, object to processing where applicable, and
      complain to your local data-protection authority. We may need to verify
      account ownership before acting. Do not post personal data in public
      GitHub issues.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      This notice describes an evolving early-stage app. Material changes to
      data handling will be reflected here with a new update date before the new
      functionality is offered.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
